# Temporary "coming soon" gate. Every URL on the domain serves the
# coming-soon content while keeping its own address bar URL (status 200 =
# rewrite, not a redirect) — so worthkeeping.info shows it directly, not
# worthkeeping.info/coming-soon.
#
# The underlying file is a flat top-level file (coming-soon.html), not a
# folder — folders (e.g. /coming-soon/, backed by index.html) are subject to
# Cloudflare's directory<->index.html canonicalization, which made every
# version of that rule look self-referential to Wrangler's deploy-time
# loop detector.
#
# The destination below is the extension-less clean URL (/coming-soon), NOT
# /coming-soon.html. Cloudflare's asset server also auto-redirects requests
# for the literal *.html file to its clean-URL form — pointing the rewrite
# at the .html path triggered that redirect on every request, straight back
# into this same catch-all, live at runtime (visible as endless 307s to
# /coming-soon, confirmed via curl). Pointing at the already-canonical
# /coming-soon avoids that extra hop entirely.
#
# These specific-path rules must stay above the catch-all: Cloudflare
# evaluates rules top-to-bottom and stops at the first match, so anything
# the coming-soon page itself loads (its own CSS/JS/images) needs to be
# excluded here or it would get swept into the rewrite too and come back
# as HTML instead of CSS/JS/images.
#
# Listed explicitly rather than as a /assets/* splat: the splat form
# (/assets/* -> /assets/:splat) deployed without error but didn't reliably
# exclude assets at runtime — favicon.svg and og-image.jpg were still
# coming back as the coming-soon HTML. Exact-path rules are what's actually
# verified working (via curl against the live deployment) for every other
# passthrough here, so asset exceptions use the same proven pattern. Add a
# new line here if the coming-soon page ever references another local file.

/styles.css              /styles.css               200
/script.js               /script.js                200
/robots.txt              /robots.txt               200
/sitemap.xml             /sitemap.xml              200
/assets/favicon.svg      /assets/favicon.svg       200
/assets/og-image.jpg     /assets/og-image.jpg      200

/*                       /coming-soon                200
